{
  "id": 513405764,
  "iid": 25993,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Increase minimum Windows version to one where UTF-8 can be forced",
  "description": "Windows 10 1903 introduced support for setting the ActiveCodePage\nto UTF-8 in the application manifest, so that all the A (ANSI)\nWin32 API functions work with UTF-8. That would mean getting rid\nof a bunch of workarounds, like the cli_main.c wrapper, filesystem\nwrappers, and Lua patches.\n\nBump our required Windows 10 version from 1809 / Server 2019 (the minimums\ncurrently required by Qt) to the next major Long Term Support versions,\n21H2 and Server 2022. Versions between 1809 and Server 2019 are already\nEoL.[1],[2]. Win 10 1809 and Server 2019 can continue to use Wireshark 4.6.x.\n\nThis will also require a change on the website to prevent the updater\nfrom downloading this version.\n\nPing #20501\n\n[1] - https://endoflife.date/windows\n[2] - https://endoflife.date/windows-server",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-07-30T13:20:14.684Z",
